#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate leakage-aware hard benchmarks for the complete name-reading layer.

The existing focused OCR set is valuable regression evidence, but it is small
and concentrated on the twelve newest grapheme rules.  This generator builds
four separate datasets from source registries and the frozen catalog without
reading search results:

* atomic accuracy: one declared mapping at a controlled catalog position;
* composed accuracy: two independent error mechanisms in one query;
* safety: exact-name collisions and queries with multiple labels generated by
  the same operation fingerprint;
* diagnostics: broader cross-rule collisions that are not equally supported;
* source boundaries: depth, length, non-transitivity, first-character scope,
  and variant-cap contracts that are more precise than a black-box rank test.

Every query collision connects its possible source families before the split
is assigned.  Consequently, a family connected through any generated query
cannot appear in development on one row and holdout on another row.
"""

